{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781496103,"nonce":"hZsibN0g0L9oCNyDLdKHtBZUltQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFd9scw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/274","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat annunciator: surface RTCM/NTRIP status (verify diag at runtime; relabel NTRIP→RTCM/NTRIP)","message":"## Observation (2026-06-12 Massabesic shakedown)\nOperator: \"the annunciator used to show RTCM data status.\" During the shakedown\nthe RTCM/correction status wasn't apparent on the annunciator.\n\n## Finding — the indicators already exist; this is a runtime/recognizability gap\nThe boat annunciator config **already defines** the relevant tiles\n(`bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat_annunciator.yaml`):\n- `RTK` → `diagnostic_name: \"GPS: RTK\"` (line 49)\n- `NTRIP` → `diagnostic_name: \"NTRIP\"` (line 54)\n\nNothing was removed from config, so the likely causes are:\n1. **Runtime:** the NTRIP diagnostic (\"NTRIP\", from the ntrip diagnostics node)\n   wasn't being published at the lake → the `NTRIP` tile sat stale/unknown, OR\n2. **Recognizability:** the operator was looking for a tile labelled \"RTCM\" and\n   didn't map it to the `NTRIP` / `RTK` tiles.\n\n## Actions\n- **Verify at runtime** that the `NTRIP` diagnostic and `GPS: RTK` diagnostic are\n  actually published (and reaching the operator `/diagnostics`) during a session.\n- **Relabel for clarity:** rename the `NTRIP` tile → **`RTCM/NTRIP`** so the\n  correction-stream status is recognizable at a glance (one-line config change).\n- If the NTRIP diagnostic is missing at runtime, trace whether the ntrip\n  diagnostics node is launched in the field config.\n\n## Note\nCompanion to the other annunciator runtime observation from this debrief (boat\nStarlink tile blank). **If the boat→operator `/diagnostics` relay is dropping\nboat-side entries, these may share a single root cause** — worth checking the\nrelay before treating them as independent.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Correction status is visible and correctly labelled on the annunciator during a\n  live session; a present/absent RTCM stream is distinguishable at a glance.\n\nSource: 2026-06-12 Massabesic shakedown debrief (operator-UX quick win E2).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}